        "original_id": "80505125-82ed-5264-bad7-5d0c4f8c0186",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Glenn Quagmire, Seth MacFarlane, Brian Griffin, Cheryl Tiegs\n- Roles: show creator, voice actor, actress\n- Works: Family Guy, Ted, A Million Ways to Die in the West, Ted 2, \"Tiegs for Two\"\n- Concepts: 1950s party-animal clichés, rat-pack era\n\nFacts:\n- Seth MacFarlane wrote, directed, and starred in the film \"Ted\" in 2012.\n- Seth MacFarlane wrote, directed, and starred in the film \"A Million Ways to Die in the West\" in 2014.\n- Seth MacFarlane wrote, directed, and starred in the film \"Ted 2\" in 2015.\n- Seth MacFarlane, the show creator and voice actor, described Glenn Quagmire as \"an appalling human being who is still caught in the rat-pack era\" and said the character is based on anachronistic 1950s party-animal clichés.\n- In the \"Family Guy\" episode \"Tiegs for Two,\" Brian Griffin again fails to get a date and seeks advice from his sex-crazed neighbor Glenn Quagmire.\n- In \"Tiegs for Two,\" Glenn Quagmire is pursuing his ex-lover, the actress Cheryl Tiegs.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
